  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Douane beach is one of the small beaches and coves that extend L'Escalet towards Cap Taillat, along Ramatuelle's coastal path. It takes its name from the customs house (maison des Douanes) standing right by the water, built under Napoleon I and recently restored. Its white sand is among the most beautiful on the French Riviera, with a direct view of Cap Taillat — the Ramatuelle tourist office ranks it among the municipality's "most beautiful beaches".</p>

      <h2>Good to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the Ramatuelle tourist office's 2025 "Dog friendly" leaflet, all the municipality's beaches (Pampelonne, Bonne Terrasse, L'Escalet and the coves) are open to dogs on a leash. The leaflet mentions no period or time slot, and no municipal order was found online: if in doubt, call the tourist office (04 98 12 64 00). Swimming is allowed except in swimming-only zones (ZRUB). La Douane beach has no lifeguard (tourist office) and can only be reached on foot. As the Cap Taillat site is protected, stay on the marked paths and keep your dog on a leash (Conservatoire du littoral / CEN Paca).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: start from L'Escalet car park and follow the coastal path (yellow markers); La Douane beach lies at the foot of the Cap Taillat peninsula, near the customs house. Bring water for your dog.</div>

      <p>The tourist office pages for Pampelonne and L'Escalet beaches state that dogs on a leash are allowed all year round. The "Plage de l'Escalet - isthme du cap Taillat" route page (Visit Var, updated by the tourist office on 06/02/2026) says "animals accepted" and free access all year. The walk starts at L'Escalet car park, next to the tennis courts: walk up the boulevard to the cul-de-sac, where the coastal trail starts and joins the coastal path. At La Douane point, a path climbs to the isthmus and an old watchtower with a 360° view; you return the same way. The leaflet states that on the coastal path, dogs on a leash are tolerated as long as they stay on the path.</p>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <h3>Are dogs allowed on La Douane beach?</h3>
      <p>Yes, on a leash, according to the Ramatuelle tourist office, as on the municipality's other beaches; the leaflet gives no dates or hours.</p>
      <h3>Is there a water point?</h3>
      <p>No water point is mentioned along the way by the sources consulted — remember to bring water for your dog.</p>
      <h3>How do you get to La Douane beach?</h3>
      <p>On foot only, via the coastal path, starting from L'Escalet beach car park (paid from 2 April to 4 October 2026).</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The path continues towards <a href="/fiche-plage-cap-taillat">Cap Taillat</a>. For an easier beach, head to <a href="/en/fiche-pampelonne">Pampelonne beach</a> or <a href="/en/fiche-bonne-terrasse">Bonne Terrasse beach</a>. <a href="/en/fiche-escalet">L'Escalet beach</a>, a family beach about 350 m long (tourist office), is the starting point of the path.</p>
